<p class="eyebrow">The launch film</p>
<h2>Break. Fix. Prove.</h2>
<p class="lede" style="margin-top:0">One quickstart, one broken step, one proof. 44 seconds.</p>
<video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="assets/launch-poster.jpg" aria-label="FirstRun launch film, 44 seconds">
<source src="assets/firstrun-launch.mp4" type="video/mp4">
<a href="assets/firstrun-launch.mp4">Download the launch film (MP4, 6 MB)</a>
</video>
<p class="cap">Posted on X on Sat Oct 10, 2026. <a href="https://twitter.com/cultist_dev/status/2108828983194206308">See the post</a>. Built solo for neatHack, the neatlogs hackathon, Oct 10 to 12, 2026.</p>
</section>

<section id="how">
<h2>Read. Run. Prove.</h2>
<p class="lede" style="margin-top:0">The same three moves every time.</p>
<div class="rrp">
<div><figure><img src="assets/step-run.webp" alt="A terminal command, firstrun run with a docs URL, above six numbered quickstart steps in a clean container" width="910" height="510" loading="lazy"></figure><h3>Read</h3><p>Give it a docs URL. FirstRun reads the page and plans one step per command.</p></div>
<div><figure><img src="assets/step-3.webp" alt="Six quickstart steps. The first two pass and step 3, run demo, fails for a new developer" width="1060" height="420" loading="lazy"></figure><h3>Run</h3><p>Every step runs in a clean container, like a new developer. The first failure stops the run.</p></div>
<div><figure><img src="assets/step-prove.webp" alt="Break, Fix, Prove: step 3 of 6 fails, the docs fix is applied, a second clean container passes 6 of 6 steps" width="980" height="330" loading="lazy"></figure><h3>Prove</h3><p>A fix is not done until a second clean container passes the whole quickstart.</p></div>
</div>
