<p class="eyebrow">Powered by neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai</p>
<h2>Three Tools. One Job Each.</h2>
<p class="lede" style="margin-top:0">The three tools of the hackathon sit inside FirstRun. Each one does one job, and the screenshots below come from this build.</p>
<div class="tools">
<article class="tool"><div class="txt">
<header><img class="lg" src="assets/logo-neatlogs.webp" alt="neatlogs logo" width="44" height="44"><h3>neatlogs</h3></header>
<p class="job">Traces every run.</p>
<p>The planner, executor and verifier show up as spans, so a bad run has a cause you can read.</p>
<a class="more" href="https://neatlogs.com">neatlogs.com</a></div>
<figure><img src="assets/shot-neatlogs.webp" alt="neatlogs trace of the FirstRun planner: 3 steps in 12 seconds, with the runbook JSON it produced" loading="lazy" width="1300" height="572"><figcaption>The first FirstRun trace, Sat Oct 10.</figcaption></figure>
</article>
<article class="tool"><div class="txt">
<header><img class="lg" src="assets/logo-entire.webp" alt="Entire logo" width="44" height="44"><h3>Entire</h3></header>
<p class="job">Records every session.</p>
<p>Each commit carries the Claude Code session that wrote it, so any line traces to a prompt.</p>
<a class="more" href="https://entire.io">entire.io</a></div>
<figure><img src="assets/shot-entire.webp" alt="Entire trails view for the firstrun repository with trail number 1 in Planning" loading="lazy" width="1300" height="484"><figcaption>Trail #1 for the firstrun repo.</figcaption></figure>
</article>
